<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήπου</span></b> , indef. Adv. (better written
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δή που</span></b> ) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>perhaps, it may be,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾧ δή που ἀδελφεὸν ἔκτανε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.736
				</span></i>
			: in Trag. and 
				Att.
			 usu. <i>doubtless, I presume,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ δήπου τλητόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1064
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Ααΐου δ. τις ὠνομάζετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1042
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				491
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				582
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.121
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴστε γὰρ δή που, μέμνησθε
				γὰρ δή που,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				2.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.113
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				18.249
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδὸν ἴσμεν ἅπαντες δή που</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδεὶς ἀγνοεῖ δή που</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					21.156
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> asinterrog.
			implying an affirm. answer, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν αἰχμάλωτον
				κάτοισθα δή που;</span> i.e. <i>I presume</i> you know,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				418
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνόμοιον δή που</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					159b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ δή που;</span>
			<i>surely it is</i> not <i>so?</i> implying a neg. answer, as
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				526
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Men.</u>
				73c
			</span></i>.</div>
